  "description": "<p>org.fcrepo.client.FedoraClient internally uses a instance of org.apache.http.impl.client.CloseableHttpClient to execute requests.</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>The development tutorial for HttpClient 4.5.x states in section 1.2.2 (<a href=\"https://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-client-4.5.x/current/tutorial/html/fundamentals.html#d5e217):\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://hc.apache.org/httpcomponents-client-4.5.x/current/tutorial/html/fundamentals.html#d5e217):</a></p>\n\n<p>\"When an instance <tt>CloseableHttpClient</tt> is no longer needed and is about to go out of scope the connection manager associated with it must be shut down by calling the <tt>CloseableHttpClient#close()</tt> method.\"</p>\n\n<p> <br/>\nTherefore FedoraClient should implement java.io.Closable to correctly shutdown the connection manager associated with the HttpClient.</p>",
